.TH DEVFIX 1 "August 2026" "DevFix 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
devfix \- built-in developer-network routing for Intel macOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B devfix
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
DevFix diagnoses developer-network failures and routes selected command-line tools through direct networking or a bundled Tor/Snowflake transport. It does not require an existing VPN or proxy and does not modify macOS system-wide proxy or DNS settings.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor [--verbose]
Inspect system, developer tools, direct endpoint reachability, transport availability, and legacy Homebrew compatibility.
.TP
.B connect [auto|direct|snowflake|external-proxy]
Establish a developer route. Auto prefers direct access and falls back to bundled Snowflake.
.TP
.B disconnect
Stop DevFix-owned transport processes and clear runtime state.
.TP
.B status
Display connection and transport state.
.TP
.B repair
Remove stale DevFix runtime state.
.TP
.B transport list|status|auto|test
Inspect and test route backends.
.TP
.B brew ARGS...
Run Homebrew inside the selected DevFix route and classify common failures.
.TP
.B git ARGS...
Run Git inside the selected route.
.TP
.B curl ARGS...
Run curl inside the selected route.
.TP
.B run COMMAND [ARGS...]
Run another CLI command inside the selected route.
.TP
.B proxy set URL
Configure an optional external HTTP/SOCKS proxy fallback.
.TP
.B logs [--tail N]
Show DevFix and Tor notice logs.
.TP
.B uninstall [--purge]
Run the installed uninstaller. Purge also removes per-user DevFix state and logs.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/DevFix
Per-user configuration, Tor data, and runtime state.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Logs/DevFix
DevFix and Tor logs.
.TP
.I /usr/local/libexec/devfix/tor
Bundled Tor Expert Bundle payload.
.SH SECURITY
DevFix does not intentionally disable TLS verification, install root certificates, edit /etc/hosts, disable Gatekeeper or SIP, or permanently change system network settings.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Snowflake is a censorship-circumvention transport, not a performance guarantee. It may be slower than direct networking and may not work on every network. DevFix cannot fix software that no longer supports the installed macOS version.
